    {
      "id": "F-s3-unreadable-record-creates-unrecordable-vm",
      "boundaryId": "s3-named-vms",
      "criterionIds": [
        "VM-1",
        "VM-2"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** with the record unreadable (`guests.json` unparsable or unreadable), `rayx setup --lima [--vm <name>]` must not create a VM it cannot record, because a VM missing from the record is now never adopted. The guest-layer invariant is that a failed read is never presented as an empty record, and the migration already guards the same hazard (`migrate_lima` calls `records::update_guests(.., |_| {})` and stops before any stop/rename when the record cannot be read or written).\n\n**Observed:** `lima::run_with` turns a failed `records::read_guests` into `GuestsFile::default()` and keeps the error in `unreadable`, but only uses it to word the never-adopt refusal for an already existing VM. When the VM does not exist (and no migration is pending), the `None` branch runs `limactl create` and `limactl start` and the guest steps; `guest::record_run` then fails on the same unreadable record (`records::record_guest` -> `read_guests_at` error, only printed, 'never fails the run'). Result: a VM that rayx just created is unrecorded. The next run refuses it as `<name> exists in Lima and rayx cannot tell whether it created it`, and once the owner repairs or deletes `guests.json` it is refused as `exists in Lima but was not created by rayx`, so the owner has to delete the VM rayx made by hand. Before this sprint nothing refused such a VM, so the trap is new with never-adopt. The same default-empty read also hides an interrupted migration's retired entry from `pending_lima`, so a new `<name>` is created from scratch instead of resuming. No test covers creation with an unreadable record (the only unreadable-record test starts from an existing VM).\n\n**Repair:** in `run_with`, when `unreadable` is `Some` and the run is not `--check`, and the VM is about to be created (existing is `None`), return `LimaError::Failed` with the record error and an instruction to fix or remove the file, before `sizing::customize` / `limactl create` (the same condition as the migration guard; `--check` may still print the plan). Add a test to `tests/lima_named_vms.rs`: unparsable `guests.json`, no VM in Lima, name `app` and `rayx` -> error carries the record problem, `limactl_lines` is empty (nothing created or started), record file left untouched.",
